    51	
    52	**$\Gamma$ is a linear subspace of $\mathbb{R}^{n}$** ([[def-linear-subspace]]).
    53	It is nonempty: $\langle 0, x_k\rangle = 0$ for every $k$ by bilinearity, and the
    54	series with all terms $0$ converges. For $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}$ and
    55	$a, b \in \Gamma$, bilinearity and the absolute value laws give
    56	
    57	$$\bigl|\langle \lambda a + b, x_k\rangle\bigr| \;=\; \bigl|\lambda\langle a,x_k\rangle + \langle b,x_k\rangle\bigr| \;\le\; |\lambda|\,\bigl|\langle a,x_k\rangle\bigr| + \bigl|\langle b,x_k\rangle\bigr|$$
    58	
    59	([[lem-of-abs-value]]), and the series of the right-hand side converges by
    60	[[lem-series-linearity]] clauses 1 and 2, so the left-hand series converges by
    61	the comparison test ([[thm-direct-comparison-test]], the terms being
    62	nonnegative). By the one-step subspace test
    63	([[lem-linear-subspace-criterion]]), $\Gamma$ is a linear subspace.
    64	
    65	**$\Gamma^{\perp}$ is a linear subspace of $\mathbb{R}^{n}$.** It contains $0$,
