    67	bilinearity gives $\langle a, \lambda y + z\rangle = \lambda\langle a,y\rangle + \langle a,z\rangle = 0$;
    68	again [[lem-linear-subspace-criterion]] applies. Equivalently $\Gamma^{\perp}$ is
    69	the intersection of the linear subspaces
